# Line endings, settled once.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Without it, Git on Windows converts LF to CRLF on
# checkout, and anything that runs `git add -A` across the repo then commits
# every converted file as changed. On 2026-07-27 the Obsidian Git plugin did
# exactly that: commit 83ac9d8, titled "notes", rewrote 24 source files and
# changed ZERO characters of content (`git diff -w` was empty). It then
# conflicted with every real change in flight, and the conflict looked like a
# genuine one - every line of every file, on both sides.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises to LF in the repository AND in the working
# tree, so there is nothing left to convert and nothing left to churn. Node,
# Next, vitest and every editor in use handle LF on Windows without complaint.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
